Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 16:24:18 2026 -0700

    Let a host application set OrcaSlicer's accent colour

    OrcaSlicer's accent, the teal behind ColorRGB::ORCA() and
    ColorRGBA::ORCA(), is now read from ColorRGB::orca_accent(), which
    defaults to the same teal and can be set. Two load-time copies of it now
    read it at use instead, with their call sites unchanged:
    ImGuiWrapper::COL_ORCA (a macro over the new col_orca()) and IMSlider's
    BRAND_COLOR. ImGui's style table, filled once when ImGuiWrapper is
    constructed, can be filled again through ImGuiWrapper::reset_style().

    apply_brand_palette sets the accent to the action colour from the tokens
    and refills the style table, after start-up and on each appearance change.
    That recolours the ImGui and GL layer's accent: the preview sliders'
    handles, filled track and value text, gizmo highlights, the selection
    rectangle. The sliders' greys, value boxes and handle shape stay
    OrcaSlicer's.
